 "notes": {
  "textContent_sites": "These uses set .textContent (not innerHTML) so an SVG cannot be dropped in without a JS edit beyond the permitted scope: landing.html 836/841/846 (● ○ status dot), schedule.html 366/597 (→ chip), zone_setup.html 947/956 (⊙ trimming/trim), toasts with ✓ (zone_setup 953/971, schedule 677). Leave those as text or restyle the glyph via CSS.",
  "innerHTML_sites_ok": "Safe to swap for <svg class=\"i\"><use href=\"#i-NAME\"/></svg>: landing 472-478 template, 615 (zap), 687/693/698 (square / cloud-rain), 748 (paw, concatenated into textContent later -- leave as text), 911 (dot); fs 272/279/283; zone_setup 370 (thermometer array -> innerHTML); winter banners line ~37-40 on every page.",
  "sizes": "CSS: svg.i{width:18px;height:18px;fill:none;stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.8;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;flex:none}. play and dot carry their own fill=\"currentColor\"; pause carries stroke-width=\"3\" -- both exactly as Hearth does it.",
  "alternatives": "send (paper plane) is included if the implementer prefers a literal plane for Speed cal instead of gauge. star4 is the bare 4-point star Hearth uses on its Magic tab; sparkle adds the small plus like Hearth P.sparkle.",
  "hearth_key_names": "Hearth P keys renamed to canonical names: drop->droplet, snow->snowflake, rain->cloud-rain, storm->cloud-storm, partly->cloud-sun, bolt->zap, stop->square, cal->calendar, left/right/up/down->chevron-*, thermo->thermometer, cam->camera, prev/next->skip-back/skip-forward, eyeoff->eye-off, shield->shield-check."
 }
